<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nasiriyah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1870s</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Al-Nasiriyah</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nasiriyah is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> and the capital of Dhi Qar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/governorate">Governorate</a>. It was founded in the early 1870s by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nasir-pasha-al-sadun">Nasir Pasha al-Sa'dun</a>, chief of the Muntafiq confederation, as the seat of the new Ottoman sanjak, and named after him. The ruins of the Sumerian city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ur">Ur</a> lie nearby.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nasiriyah.jpg" alt="Nasiriyah" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ahmed R.D · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D9%85%D8%AF%D9%8A%D9%86%D8%A9_%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%86%D8%A7%D8%B5%D8%B1%D9%8A%D8%A9_%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AD%D8%A8%D9%88%D8%A8%D9%8A.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
